{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"mobile-groovy-badger","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`/health` on the MCP server returns 200 without ever touching the ticket store, so a container\nwith **no store at all** passes both the container HEALTHCHECK and the blue-green readiness\ngate. A structurally broken deploy is indistinguishable from a healthy one.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:118-120` — the handler returns `JSONResponse({\"in_flight\": gauge.value})`\n  and nothing else.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:56-57` — the container HEALTHCHECK is a plain 200 check on\n  `/health`.\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130` — the blue-green readiness gate promotes on that same probe.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:759-761` — the boot sweep is guarded by `if os.path.isdir(_tracker)`\n  and emits NOTHING when the store is absent; the comment at `:752` states the intent\n  (\"a missing store / import / sweep error never aborts boot\"), so not even the `debug` line at\n  `:769` fires (that needs an exception).\n\nCorroborating log evidence: 60 SSM invocations spanning 2026-08-06 to 2026-08-25 contain zero\nmatches for `tickets-tracker`, `not initialized`, or `ticket init` — exactly what the code\npredicts. (Container logs use `driver: journald` at `docker-compose.yml:72,258,306,383` and no\nCloudWatch log group exists for them, so there is no remote log trail either.)\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the reason the missing-store defect went unnoticed since deployment. Log-and-continue on\nboot is a defensible posture on its own; combining it with a health probe that cannot observe the\nstore means nothing in the pipeline can ever report the failure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The readiness signal distinguishes \"serving with a usable store\" from \"serving with no\n      store\" — either `/health` reports store status, or a separate readiness endpoint does and\n      the autodeploy gate consumes it.\n- [ ] Whatever the store decision in the sibling provisioning ticket, boot emits at least one log\n      line naming the store path and whether it was found.\n- [ ] Coverage asserts a storeless container does not pass the readiness gate (when a store is\n      expected).","id":"d9ab-7b5e-fe4c-4ff4","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["infra","mcp","observability","deploy"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP /health returns 200 with no ticket store, so a storeless deploy passes the blue-green readiness gate"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787706121968794001,"uuid":"12813bbd-6ff7-42b7-ab9a-659782b37e25"}